PRETABLE -- #568 (vmedefaultkill), written BEFORE kill table 1 runs (this file's mtime is the order proof).
Main loop, 2026-10-20 ~20:1x.  Fix under test: scratchpad vme/fix/dev_vme.fix568.c (md5 4e3e7fc2), generated from HEAD
by mk_fix568.py.  Detector under test: vme_default_probe.py REVISION 2 (being built by the probe sub-agent from
pass1_20261020/ADJUDICATION_p1.md plus two refinements: two announce sessions `p2 ann rd` / `p2 ann wr`; non-word
first accesses; cased write paths; interim pins; population-1 width variety).  Row names below are the PLANNED names;
when revision 2 lands its row list is DIFFED against this file's prescribed rows (the #490 rule) and any rename or
drop is recorded in an addendum written before table 1.

== 1. SIBLING PARITY ==
* The edited `default:` arm (now FAULT) vs its siblings in the same switch: the five cased debug-only arms (GCSRCTL,
  TCR, IRQEN, IRQL3, IRQL4) DECLINE with an UNLATCHED debug() per access.  The new population-2 arm DECLINES with a
  LATCHED fatal() -- owner-ruled (S3), so the asymmetry is deliberate.  Rows owed: the free-running announce rows (the
  new arm prints at default verbosity) and `free quiet` (a cased debug-only read prints NOTHING free-running) -- the
  pair pins that the two declining shapes differ in exactly the ruled way.
* The new population-2 arm vs `#501`'s PCC2 `default:` (dev_pcc2.c, the ruled sibling): same N=1-per-offset latch,
  same direction-decides-wording, same (once) marker.  `#501` disclosed its len-8 value truncation; #568 prints all 64
  bits -> row owed: a `st.d` first access whose high and low words differ (revision 2, item 2b).
* The new FAULT arm vs `dev_unreadable.c` (the pure FAULT member installed three times around this window): both
  `return 0`; dev_unreadable is silent, and #568's default keeps two debug() lines (silent free-running, measured by the
  probe sub-agent: 8 free-running population-1 faults print 0 host lines).  No asymmetry a row is owed for.

